[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Open Dashboard
Comment=Opens the calorie/macro/spending tracker dashboard
Exec=bash -c 'cd "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CLONE_PATH" && ./app/open_dashboard.sh'
Terminal=true
Icon=utilities-terminal
Categories=Utility;

# UNTESTED: written without a Linux machine available to verify against.
#
# EDIT BEFORE FIRST USE: replace REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CLONE_PATH above with
# the absolute path to wherever you cloned this repo (e.g.
# /home/you/project-for-your-health). A .desktop file can't reliably
# discover its own location across desktop environments the way a
# macOS .command file can, so this has to be set by hand once.
#
# After editing, you likely also need to mark this file executable
# (chmod +x) and, in GNOME/Nautilus specifically, right-click it and
# choose "Allow Launching" the first time - most file managers refuse to
# run a .desktop file from an untrusted location otherwise. If double-
# click launching doesn't work on your desktop environment, the reliable
# fallback is just running ./app/open_dashboard.sh directly from a
# terminal.
